-- Schema version 3 to 4 (Phase 2, PR 5b, ADR 0066).
--
-- A snooze records when it ends. The end is a derived instant, decided once when she snoozes from the snooze
-- duration then in force, and recorded with the event, as MISSED records its effectiveAt (ADR 0030). Selection,
-- the watchdog and the fire path read it and never her current setting, so changing the setting while a snooze
-- runs does not move it, and a server that mirrors events but not settings still knows when the snooze ends.
--
-- The column follows the sparse convention of the event table: nullable, and allowed on SNOOZED alone (the
-- decode guard, ADR 0052). ADD COLUMN works on the SQLite 3.22 floor (ADR 0042).
--
-- A SNOOZED event written before this version has no end. Its end is its own timestamp plus ten minutes, the
-- default snooze duration, which is what was in force for every snooze the app has recorded: no setting screen
-- exists yet, so no snooze was taken with another duration. This UPDATE is part of a migration, an
-- administrative path outside the domain layer, and not a state transition (invariant 4).

ALTER TABLE event ADD COLUMN snoozed_until INTEGER;

UPDATE event
SET snoozed_until = device_timestamp + 600000
WHERE event_type = 'SNOOZED' AND snoozed_until IS NULL;
